e book is  very psychological i talked to a lot of  psychiatrists about fidel i put quotes  from them in i never made a judgment  though on what kind of a psyche this man  has because that's much too complicated  i'm a journalist i'm not a psychiatrist  but what i tried to show  above all was how he  wove the spell  over the cuban people  also over individuals as you say like  american journalists american  activists  europeans  and i was trying to go in what is the  spell the exchange  of power so that that picture of the  masses in the  in the in the plaza in in  in havana that's where he gets his  energy that's where he gets his love  it's a tremendous exchange going on  there when they shout for him  that's where he gets his sustenance and  his love and when he  teaches them and talks to them  that's where they get it but then  i mean you stood there away 66 and  listened to him for 10 hours exactly  why would anybody do that well that's  what started me on this i you know i was  up with the foreign guests we were in a  comfortable place we could go in and out  we could talk we could chat or we could  go out and get a beer  but the  masses of cubans in the plaza they  couldn't leave at all they stood there  for nine ten hours  listening in the hot sun all day  and that was what i wanted to figure out  why was that going on does he keep  talking constantly for 10 hours  constantly does he have a script  no he doesn't he when he was younger and  i traced this uh he used to he spoke  from notes  but  by the time he came to power  it's like something gets going in him  like this passion gets going and he gets  up there and  he's just telling people everything  and  teaching them and admonishing them and  sometimes amusing them  and then they would say to me over and  over  well fidel would start to talk and  suddenly he was saying  he was saying what i have always thought  and you know and this is the exchange  it's like he's defining the world for  them and now tha